WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
Start with the part you can observe.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
Follow the relationship as it changes.

00:24.000 --> 00:36.000
A clutch uses friction surfaces to connect engine torque to the gearbox. During engagement, slip converts some energy into heat.

00:36.000 --> 00:48.000
If the two sides rotate at different speeds, the clutch is still slipping; equal speed means it is locked in this simplified model.

00:48.000 --> 01:00.000
Cause-and-effect sequence

01:00.000 --> 01:12.000
This ideal mechanism leaves out friction, temperature and part-specific behavior. Real designs need measurements.

